            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "estaman"
            },
            "reviewBody": "THIS WAS AN AWESOME RECIPE, I did alter it by leaving out the parm and added a 1/4 finley chopped onion and two garlic cloves. Egg washed them, breaded the mushroom caps before deep frying till golden brown. I did sprinkle grated parm over the top when they came out of the fryer. \nAWESOME, AWESOME, AWESOME!!!",
            "datePublished": "2013-11-29T12:26:37.607Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Dean"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I checked the other reviews first, so I made some adjustments. Put the stems in the mix, I didn't want to waste them. I also added some fresh parsely and garlic. Turned out great! I also put some breadcrumbs on top and broiled for the last couple of minutes. Everyone loved them. I will be making these again.",
            "datePublished": "2020-01-13T22:25:14.177Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mac"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have made this many times. Each time I chop up the stems and sauté them in a little bit of the bacon grease along with some with finely diced onion and garlic. Then i add that to the stuffing mixture. It intensifies the mushroom flavor.",
            "datePublished": "2016-02-15T09:03:35.393Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
